PF_PAE_ENABLED is FALSE under Rosetta 2; 64-bit Windows always reports TRUE.

Wine fills IsProcessorFeaturePresent(PF_PAE_ENABLED), and the ProcessorFeatures
array in KUSER_SHARED_DATA, from CPUID leaf 1 EDX bit 6. Rosetta's leaf 1 leaves
that bit clear, but long mode runs on PAE paging, so no x64 Windows has ever
returned FALSE. On x86_64 the feature is now always TRUE.

Not in build.sh's PATCHES list and not in fixes/: it is unconditional, so it
would change FIFA 17's ntdll, and it has not been tested with FIFA 17.
Independent of every other patch (dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c only).

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
@@ -490,6 +490,11 @@
     do_cpuid( 0x00000001, 0, regs ); /* get cpu features */
     features[PF_RDTSC_INSTRUCTION_AVAILABLE]   = !!(regs[3] & (1 << 4));
     features[PF_PAE_ENABLED]                   = !!(regs[3] & (1 << 6));
+#ifdef __x86_64__
+    /* long mode runs on PAE paging, and 64-bit Windows always reports it;
+     * Rosetta 2's CPUID leaf 1 leaves the bit clear */
+    features[PF_PAE_ENABLED]                   = TRUE;
+#endif
     features[PF_MMX_INSTRUCTIONS_AVAILABLE]    = !!(regs[3] & (1 << 23));
     features[PF_XMMI_INSTRUCTIONS_AVAILABLE]   = (regs[3] & (1 << 24)) && (regs[3] & (1 << 25));
     features[PF_XMMI64_INSTRUCTIONS_AVAILABLE] = !!(regs[3] & (1 << 26));
